{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Plan-review Pass-2 `prerequisite_verify` fails on Bedrock \"Grammar compilation timed out\"\n\n## The defect (root cause PROVEN — see the RCA comments)\n\n[rebar:18ae-27e9-b651-4b71] (commit `6c8daf7945`, 2026-08-05 00:48) added an exact-model-id row to\n`_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` in `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py`:\n\n    \"us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\": {\"native_structured_output\": True, ...}\n\nThat row is applied AFTER the `_REBAR_OVERRIDES` family rule (`_is_claude -> False`) and therefore\nwins, flipping this model from `PromptedOutput` to `NativeOutput`. rebar consequently began sending\nBedrock a JSON Schema for constrained decoding. Anthropic compiles that schema into a grammar and\nenforces a documented **180-second compilation timeout** plus complexity caps (**24 optional\nparameters**, 16 union-typed). rebar's verification contracts carry **22-36 optional parameters** —\nevery field declares a `default=`, so every field is optional in JSON Schema — and the compile\nexceeds the ceiling. Bedrock returns HTTP 400 `ValidationException`, either \"Grammar compilation\ntimed out\" (~185s) or \"Schema is too complex\" (~50-60s).\n\nResult: the Pass-2 verify step cannot run, every finding degrades to `no-verification`, the review\nlands INDETERMINATE and unsigned, and the ticket cannot be claimed.\n\n**Scale:** 27 live 400s across ~9 review targets; zero before 00:48. Affects BOTH gates — plan-review\n(`plan_review_verification`, 31 optionals) and the Gerrit `LLM-Review` code-review gate\n(`code_review_verification`, 36 optionals, pinned `model: standard` = sonnet-4-6 at\n`gates/code-review.yaml`).\n\nMeasured (live, us-east-1, serial, one variable at a time):\n\n    review_result             10 optional  NATIVE  OK      14.0s\n    completion_verdict        14 optional  NATIVE  OK      29.0s\n    verification              22 optional  NATIVE  FAIL   185.3s   <- fails UNDER the documented cap\n    plan_review_verification  31 optional  NATIVE  FAIL   185.4s\n    code_review_verification  36 optional  NATIVE  FAIL   185.4s\n    plan_review_verification  (same, PROMPTED)     OK      11.2s   <- the remedy works today\n    plan_review_verification  descriptions stripped (8719->2403 B), NATIVE  FAIL  59.8s\n\n## Approach\n\nThe fix is to stop sending a grammar the provider cannot compile, and to say so clearly when we do.\nThree parts, all inside the existing seams — no new subsystem.\n\n**1. Gate native selection on schema complexity (`src/rebar/llm/structured.py`).**\n`output_mode(model_cls, caps, thinking=...)` already receives the contract class, so the decision\nbelongs there and no signature changes. Add a pure predicate\n`native_schema_supported(model_cls) -> bool` that counts OPTIONAL properties (and union-typed\nproperties) in `model_cls.model_json_schema()` and returns False above a conservative measured\nbound. `output_mode` returns `PromptedOutput` when it returns False, even if\n`caps.native_structured_output` is True. Bound is set from the measurement above (14 passes, 22\nfails) — deliberately BELOW Anthropic's published 24, because `verification` proves the published\nnumber under-predicts. The bound is a module constant with the measurement cited beside it.\n\nThis mirrors the prevailing OSS pattern: langchain-aws defaults `method=\"function_calling\"` and\nmakes native `json_schema` opt-in; instructor, llama_index, DSPy and BAML likewise do not send a\nnative grammar by default. It also restores rebar's own pre-18ae posture for the contracts that\nneed it, WITHOUT reverting 18ae's measured benefit for small contracts.\n\n**2. Classify the rejection distinctly (`src/rebar/llm/failure.py`).**\nAdd `translate_schema_complexity_rejection(exc, model_id)` returning a typed error, mirroring the\nexisting `translate_sampling_parameter_rejection` (`failure.py:371`) exactly — same conjunctive\nshape (`status_code == 400` or `ValidationException` in text, AND a documented phrase from a small\nclosed set), same \"tried FIRST in the broad except\" wiring in `structured_run.py`. The message names\nthe model, the contract, and the remedy. This is what stops a schema-complexity rejection being\nreported as an opaque provider outage (AC1).\n\n**3. Fall back rather than fail closed (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`, minimal).**\nIn `_pai_structured`, when the NativeOutput branch raises and\n`translate_schema_complexity_rejection` recognises it, log loudly and retry ONCE on the existing\nPROMPTED branch (proven to work: 11.2s). The fallback is never silent — it logs at WARNING and the\nclassified cause is attached — which answers the strongest objection to auto-fallback (TanStack/ai\n#682 stripped theirs partly because it hid the signal). Kept small because this module is at\n750/800 LOC: the predicate and message live in the two modules above, not here.\n\nRetry-without-change is deliberately NOT used: the rejection is a deterministic property of the\nrequest (27 identical failures), so a plain retry burns another ~185s and fails again.\n\n## Non-goals (explicit)\n\n* **AC3 — partial credit for a failed verify: WON'T FIX** (operator decision, 2026-08-05). The\n  degrade is deliberate: `plan_review_recovery` preserves Pass-1 findings and routes them through\n  `pass3_decide(None)`, the kernel's documented no-verification degrade, stamping\n  `verify_failed: True`. Signing over unverified findings would weaken what a plan-review\n  attestation means. Fixing the routing removes the trigger instead.\n* **Not reverting 18ae's row.** Native output demonstrably works for small contracts on this model\n  (14.0s / 29.0s measured) and 18ae's tests pin it; the row is not wrong, its scope is — it asserts\n  a model fact where the real constraint is per-schema.\n* **Not restructuring the verification contracts.** Making their fields `required` would reduce\n  optionality, but the defaults are load-bearing (an older/absent verifier must ABSTAIN, per\n  `verify_models.py`). That is a contract change, not a bug fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a Bedrock/Anthropic schema-complexity rejection (`Grammar compilation timed out` /\n      `Schema is too complex`, 400 `ValidationException`) is classified DISTINCTLY and is not\n      surfaced as a generic provider outage; the operator message names the model and the contract\n- [ ] `output_mode` returns `PromptedOutput` for a contract whose optional-parameter count exceeds\n      the measured bound, even when the model's capability record says native is available\n- [ ] the plan-review Pass-2 verify step completes against `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`\n      for the `plan_review_verification` contract (31 optionals) that reproduces the failure today\n- [ ] the same protection covers the code-review gate's `code_review_verification` contract (36\n      optionals), which is pinned to the same model class and fails identically\n- [ ] a regression test drives the classification path with a SIMULATED provider\n      grammar-compilation rejection and asserts it is not reported as an outage (no live call)\n- [ ] a test pins `output_mode`'s complexity gate with a fixture that varies BOTH poles — a\n      small contract still routes NativeOutput on a native-capable model, a large one routes\n      PromptedOutput — so the test cannot pass vacuously\n- [ ] 18ae's existing pins still pass: the measured small-contract cells keep NativeOutput\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/test_structured.py tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py -q\n    pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q\n    make lint && make typecheck\n    # live replication of the original report:\n    rebar review-plan 895c-3eb2-043a-4de1\n\n## Evidence\n\nRCA + measurements in this ticket's comments. Logs: `/tmp/rp3.log`, `/tmp/rp4.log`,\n`/tmp/c827-planreview{,2}.log`, `/tmp/4ca2_rev*_err.log`, `/tmp/03ef-review4.out` (\"Schema is too\ncomplex\"), `/tmp/rp94a3c.log`. Discovered while attempting to earn the claim attestation for\n[rebar:c827-2a23-cd00-473e]."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785957126823318001,"uuid":"6f7158d6-a129-45b8-9a36-76a8ca6823c1"}